{"name":"Beach Ball","hex":"#efc700","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"beach ball","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A large light inflatable ball, ideally suited to beach games.","A spinning wait cursor in macOS."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/beach_ball"}],"entries":[{"title":"Beach Ball","blocks":[{"text":"Beach Ball is a 1965 American beach party comedy film directed by Lennie Weinrib and starring Edd Byrnes and Chris Noel. It was partly financed by Roger Corman. It features appearances by the Supremes, the Walker Brothers, and the Righteous Brothers."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/ca/Beach_Ball_1965_film_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beach_Ball","wikidata":"Q4875675"},{"title":"Beach ball","blocks":[{"text":"A beach ball is an inflatable ball for beach and water games. Their large size and light weight require little effort to propel them."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/BeachBall.jpg/330px-BeachBall.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beach_ball","wikidata":"Q650736"},{"title":"Beach","blocks":[{"text":"A beach is a landform alongside a body of water which consists of loose particles. The particles composing a beach are typically made from rock, such as sand, gravel, shingle, pebbles, etc., or biological sources, such as mollusc shells or coralline algae. Sediments settle in different densities and structures, depending on the local wave action and weather, creating different textures, colors and gradients or layers of material."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Beach_at_Fort_Lauderdale.jpg/330px-Beach_at_Fort_Lauderdale.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beach","wikidata":"Q40080"},{"title":"Ball","blocks":[{"text":"A ball is a round object. Balls can have several uses. For example they are used in ball games, where the play of the game follows the state of the ball as it is hit, kicked or thrown by players. Balls can also be used for simpler activities, such as catch or juggling. Balls made from hard-wearing materials are used in engineering applications to provide very low friction bearings, known as ball bearings. Black-powder weapons use stone and metal balls as projectiles."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/Many_balls.jpg/330px-Many_balls.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ball","wikidata":"Q18545"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/93/%22Fantasy_of_Florida_-_Dreams_Expressed_in_Architecture%22_%2811450657393%29.jpg/500px-%22Fantasy_of_Florida_-_Dreams_Expressed_in_Architecture%22_%2811450657393%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/93/%22Fantasy_of_Florida_-_Dreams_Expressed_in_Architecture%22_%2811450657393%29.jpg/500px-%22Fantasy_of_Florida_-_Dreams_Expressed_in_Architecture%22_%2811450657393%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A couple playing with a beach ball in a 1985 Florida postcard","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A%22Fantasy_of_Florida_-_Dreams_Expressed_in_Architecture%22_(11450657393).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Lago_di_Lavarone_190820_03.jpg/500px-Lago_di_Lavarone_190820_03.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Lago_di_Lavarone_190820_03.jpg/1280px-Lago_di_Lavarone_190820_03.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"htt